From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:02:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/common/block/acpi: Give macOS plugin-type on the
 first CPU

With the CPU threads declared as Processor objects (acpi_cpu_objects),
macOS finds them, but its kernel runs XCPM, its CPU power management,
only when the first thread carries the property plugin-type 1, which
makes it load the X86PlatformPlugin. OpenCore configurations add it with
an SSDT, OpenCore's SSDT-PLUG sample, that defines _DSM on the first
CPU.

Add that _DSM to the first Processor object: for Apple's UUID
(a0b5b7c6-1318-441c-b0c9-fe695eaf949b) function 0 lists function 1,
which returns Package () { "plugin-type", 1 }; other functions and other
UUIDs get Buffer () { 0 }. No other OS asks with Apple's UUID. The
Device (ACPI0007) objects, the default, get no _DSM: macOS does not find
CPUs declared that way.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/acpi.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/acpi.c b/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/acpi.c
index 63adbd8a0d..2d3be28786 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/acpi.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/block/acpi/acpi.c
@@ -358,6 +358,25 @@ __weak void soc_power_states_generation(int core_id,
 {
 }
 
+/*
+ * The _DSM through which macOS takes device properties (Apple's UUID), on
+ * the first thread: plugin-type 1 there makes the kernel load the
+ * X86PlatformPlugin, thus XCPM, the CPU power management of macOS. It is
+ * what the SSDT-PLUG sample of OpenCore adds; no other OS asks with this
+ * UUID.
+ */
+#define APPLE_DSM_UUID	"a0b5b7c6-1318-441c-b0c9-fe695eaf949b"
+
+static void apple_dsm_plugin_type(void *arg)
+{
+	/* Return (Package () { "plugin-type", 1 }) */
+	acpigen_emit_byte(RETURN_OP);
+	acpigen_write_package(2);
+	acpigen_write_string("plugin-type");
+	acpigen_write_integer(1);
+	acpigen_write_package_end();
+}
+
 static void generate_cpu_entry(int cpu, int core, int cores_per_package, bool processor_op)
 {
 	const unsigned int index = cpu * cores_per_package + core;
@@ -380,6 +399,13 @@ static void generate_cpu_entry(int cpu, int core, int cores_per_package, bool pr
 	/* Soc specific power states generation */
 	soc_power_states_generation(core, cores_per_package);
 
+	/* macOS only finds Processor objects: plugin-type with them */
+	if (processor_op && index == 0) {
+		/* Function 0 lists function 1, the properties */
+		void (*callbacks[])(void *) = { NULL, apple_dsm_plugin_type };
+		acpigen_write_dsm(APPLE_DSM_UUID, callbacks, ARRAY_SIZE(callbacks), NULL);
+	}
+
 	if (processor_op)
 		acpigen_write_processor_end();
 	else
-- 
